From: FiberHome HG5582A port <dev@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep VLAN-unaware bridge egress untagged

The PON L2 fallback resolves the bridge egress through the pon0.<vid>
VLAN upper.  For a VLAN-unaware bridge br_fill_forward_path() leaves the
ingress VLAN in ctx, so the PPE L2B template would carry the service tag
and push it back onto the LAN port even though the software bridge sends
the VLAN upper's untagged frame.

Clear the egress VLAN stack when the bridge does not have VLAN filtering
enabled.  VLAN-aware bridges keep the stack selected by the FDB path.

Signed-off-by: FiberHome HG5582A port <dev@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1444,6 +1444,15 @@
 		return false;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A VLAN-unaware bridge forwards the untagged frame produced by the
+	 * pon0.<vid> VLAN upper.  br_fill_forward_path() leaves the ingress
+	 * VLAN in ctx for such a bridge, but the PPE egress template must not
+	 * push that tag back onto the LAN port.
+	 */
+	if (!br_vlan_enabled(master))
+		ctx.num_vlans = 0;
+
 	data.vlan.num = ctx.num_vlans;
 	for (i = 0; i < ctx.num_vlans; i++) {
 		data.vlan.hdr[i].id = ctx.vlan[i].id;
